<h3>Running it</h3>

<CodeSnippet Code="@run" />

<p class="note">
    The database is a SQLite file next to the project, seeded once with 1,000 rows shaped so every feature
    has something to do: snake_case columns, text-encoded <code>Guid</code>, <code>DateOnly</code>,
    <code>TimeOnly</code> and <code>TimeSpan</code>, nulls at regular intervals, a decimal string that a
    German culture reads as a different number, and padded text for the converter.
</p>

<p class="note">
    SQLite is the only dependency the example adds. The library itself still has none.
</p>

@code {
    private const string run = "dotnet run --project examples/DataMapper.Extensions.Web";
}
